  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer NNN, help Chef in finding an NNN-digit odd&nbsp;positive&nbsp;integer\\textbf{odd positive integer}odd&nbsp;positive&nbsp;integer XXX such that XXX is divisible by 333 but not by 999.\n\nNote:\\textbf{Note}:Note: There should not be any leading zeroes in XXX. In other words, 003003003 is not a valid 333-digit odd positive integer.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of testcases. The description of the TTT testcases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the number of digits in XXX.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output a single line containing an NNN-digit odd positive integer XXX in decimal number system, such that XXX is divisible by 333 but not by 999.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5001 \\leq T \\leq 5001≤T≤500",
      "1≤N≤1041 \\leq N \\leq 10^41≤N≤104",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n2\n3",
        "output": "3\n15\n123",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: 333 is the only 111-digit odd positive integer which is divisible by 333 but not by 999.\nTest Case 222: 151515 is a 222-digit odd positive integer which is divisible by 333 but not by 999. 212121 is also a valid answer, among others. Note that 030303 is not a valid answer as there should not be any leading zeroes in the output."
      }
    ]
  },
